T10:03:32Z","updated_at":"2026-06-15T13:56:44Z","closed_at":"2026-06-15T13:56:44Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\n- Reproducible in: 4.7.rc2 [3df26a02c]\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.7.rc2 - Windows 11 (build 26200) - Multi-window, 1 monitor - Direct3D 12 (Forward+) - dedicated NVIDIA GeForce RTX 5070 Ti (NVIDIA; 32.0.16.1047) - 13th Gen Intel(R) Core(TM) i7-13700KF (24 threads) - 31.76 GiB memory - WASAPI (48000 Hz, Stereo/mono)\n\n### Issue description\n\nSetting gravity scale on a RigidBody3D only seems to work in `_enter_tree`. So setting it in `_ready` or `_physics_process` does nothing right now.\n\nThis only applies to Jolt Physics, in Godot Physics 3D it still works as expected.\n\nReverting #118197 and #118291 fixed the problem for me, so it seems related to changes in #118197\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nUse Jolt Physics and try to set gravity_scale on a RigidBody3D from code in `_ready` or `_physics_process`. Really simple to reproduce, but did include an MRP that you can just play to see this behaviour.\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n[test.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/28910511/test.zip)","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.gi